-- VC-11 — Visit Checklist template v2 (DESIGN §9.7, §20).
--
-- One content change: the critical sweep question "Is this the actual unit
-- you'd rent, or a model?" gains a third option, `similar`. The common answer on
-- a real tour is neither of the other two — the agent walks you through the same
-- plan two floors down — and with only `actual` and `model` on offer that tour
-- was recorded as one of two wrong things.
--
-- A new version rather than an edit to the v1 rows, because `template_version`
-- is frozen into every Visit at creation: a finished Visit must keep asking
-- exactly what it asked, and its completion percentage must keep meaning what it
-- meant. v1 rows stay exactly where they are and are never touched again.
--
-- Generated by `api/src/manzil_api/visits/template.py::generate_template_sql()`.
-- `api/tests/test_visit_template.py` asserts this block still matches the module,
-- so the two cannot drift silently. Do not hand-edit.

